# THE LAST LIGHT · Chapter 5 · The Truth
# ROSS speaks in person if the door was opened, otherwise through the door (VISITOR). Both use ROSS once his name is known.

== ch5_ross mode=person
[if has_flag("door_open")] ~ He stands just inside the door and lets the water run off him onto Father's floor. He won't take the chair.
[if has_flag("door_shut")] ~ I sit with my back against the door. I can hear him breathing on the other side of two inches of oak.
ROSS: We struck at two minutes to two. I know because I was looking at the clock in the wheelhouse when the light didn't come round.
ROSS: Eight of us. The sea took the wheelhouse roof off with me holding it. I woke on the shingle on Pabbay with my hip broken and a seal looking at me.
* How did you live? -> how
* Why didn't you come back? -> why
= how
ROSS: Shellfish and rainwater, nine days. A crofter found me. I told him my name was Sandy. That's who I've been since.
-> why
= why
ROSS: Because I thought I'd killed them.
ROSS: Your father told the Inquiry the light was burning. The Board's own keeper. Who'd believe a drowned drunk over that? I didn't believe me.
ROSS: So I let Alasdair Ross stay dead. My wife was told I'd taken seven good men onto the rocks with drink. My girl grew up hearing it in the schoolyard.
ROSS: Then two years ago I'm in the Mitchell Library in Glasgow, reading the Inquiry report for the hundredth time, and I see it. Mayday logged at Stornoway at oh-one-fifty-two. "No light."
ROSS: And your father's book says the light failed at oh-two-ten.
ROSS: I wrote to the Board. Twice. They wrote back to thank me for my interest.
* My father wrote that entry. -> blame_father
* [if clue("same_hand")] I wrote that entry. -> confess
* What do you want from me? -> want
= blame_father
! set blamed_father=1
ROSS: Did he.
ROSS: Then he wrote it with your hand, Callum. I've seen your log. I watched you write it tonight through those windows with the glass full of light.
-> drawer
= confess
! set confessed_to_ross=1
! add rel.ross 2
ROSS: ...
ROSS: Aye. I know. I've known for two years.
ROSS: You were twenty-three. You did what your father told you. God help me, so did I at that age.
-> drawer
= want
ROSS: The truth in the light's own book. In your hand, since it was your hand. And I want to see my girl's ship past the Gut tonight. She's coming by at five.
-> drawer
= drawer
ROSS: Your father wrote to me once. Or to someone. Fifty-seven, it would have been, when he was dying. A man told me in Govan he'd heard of a letter that never got posted.
ROSS: Iain was a tidy man. Look in the bottom drawer of that desk.

== ch5_letter mode=thought
~ Under the old tide tables, an envelope. My name on the front, in Father's careful copperplate. Never sealed.
~ "Callum. I made you write it. I made a boy of twenty-three put his name to my lie, because I was asleep in this chair with the bottle and the light was out and I could not face it."
~ "Ross was a better man than me. If you ever have the courage I did not, put it right. Your father, Iain Mackay. Christmas 1957."
~ He died in the March.
* (Hand the letter to Ross.) -> hand
* (Fold it into your pocket.) -> keep
= hand
! set gave_letter=1
! add rel.ross 1
ROSS: ...
ROSS: He used to sing that song as well, you know. When he thought nobody could hear. Badly.
-> END
= keep
! set kept_letter=1
~ Ross watches me fold it away. He doesn't ask.

== ch5_morag mode=radio
! static
MORAG: North Point, Stornoway. Callum, talk to me. Are you safe? Over.
[if has_flag("door_open")] * He's inside. He's an old man and he's wet through. I'm safe. -> safe
[if has_flag("door_shut")] * He's still at the door. I'm safe. -> safe_door
* Morag. It's Alasdair Ross. -> ross
= safe
MORAG: Who is he, Callum?
-> ross
= safe_door
MORAG: Who is he, Callum?
= ross
MORAG: ...
MORAG: That's not possible.
[if has_flag("door_open")] ROSS: It's possible, lass. You wrote me down at eight minutes to two. I heard you say "Roger, Mary Ellen" and then nothing. You were the last voice I heard before the sea.
[if has_flag("door_shut")] CALLUM: He says you wrote him down at eight minutes to two. He says yours was the last voice he heard before the sea.
MORAG: ...I'm going to need to sit down.

== ch5_mayday mode=radio
! static heavy
ELSPETH: Mayday, Mayday, Mayday. This is Iona Star, Iona Star, Iona Star.
ELSPETH: Steering gear failed. We've rigged hand steering aft, slow to answer. Wind's setting us west onto North Point. Twelve souls aboard. Position one point two miles north-east of North Point Light. Over.
MORAG: Iona Star, Stornoway. Mayday received. Lifeboat is engaged at the Shiants, two hours. North Point Light is your nearest station. Over.
[if has_flag("door_open")] ~ Ross has his hand on the back of the chair. All the colour has gone out of his face.
[if has_flag("door_shut")] ~ Behind the door, something heavy slides down to the floor.
ROSS: That's Elspeth. That's my girl.

== ch5_dark mode=thought
! static fade
~ The engine coughs and dies. It ran too hot for too long.
~ A second later the main breaker goes with a crack like a pistol, and the room is black.
~ And overhead the light goes out.
